        title: `The Board Wants Changes`,
        situation: `You are the GRO administrator. At the board meeting, the governing body approves four changes: moving the operation to a larger campus in another part of town, shortening your published operating hours, rewriting your discipline policy, and adding a swimming pool at the new site. The board chair says to tell Licensing once the move is complete.`,
        question: `What notifications does the operation owe Licensing, and what are the timeframes?`,
        discussion: `Waiting until the move is complete would be a deficiency. Under §748.153(1), you must give written notice to your Licensing Representative as soon as possible, but at least 30 days before moving to another location [Medium-High] and at least 30 days before changing operating hours [Medium-Low]. Rewriting the discipline policy is a change to a policy required by §748.103(b), so written notice is due as soon as possible but at least 15 days before the change [Medium-Low] (§748.153(2)(A)). Construction of a swimming pool or other permanent body of water also requires notice at least 15 days before construction begins [Medium] (§748.153(2)(C)). A changed floor plan at the new campus would likewise need 15 days notice, and the move itself is governed by §745.435. Remember that notice is not approval: Licensing does not automatically approve what you report, and further steps may be required.`,
