        discussion: `No, on both counts. A provisional license holder may serve at a GRO only if, at the time of hire, the operation is not on a voluntary plan of action, on corrective action, subject to an adverse action, or pending due process for a corrective or adverse action (§748.532). Because your operation is on corrective action, the board must hire an administrator with a full license so the person can focus on improving compliance. Separately, a provisional license holder may serve as a licensed administrator at only one residential child-care operation (§748.533(c)), so the sister GRO idea fails regardless. Plan the transition: notify Licensing no later than two days after the administrator changes or the position becomes vacant [Medium-High] (§748.153(3)(A)), and if no back-up administrator is in place, remember you have 60 days from the vacancy to obtain a licensed administrator (§748.154).`,
