        discussion: `Orientation is completed before contact with children and does not count toward pre-service (§§748.831, 748.865). For general pre-service she has met the 4-hour minimum before being counted, and the remaining 4 hours are due within 30 days of becoming a caregiver (§748.863(a)(1)). For EBI, because your operation allows EBI and she serves children with emotional disorders, she needs 16 hours, with at least half (8 hours) before being counted in ratio and the rest within 90 days (§748.863(a)(3)). With only 5 EBI hours, she does not meet the threshold, so she cannot be counted yet. Even after reaching the thresholds, until all pre-service training is complete she may be counted only when a fully qualified caregiver is counted at the same time [Medium-High] (§748.863(b)). She also may not administer any EBI, other than a short personal restraint, until all 16 hours are done. In addition, she needs first aid within 90 days and CPR before being the only caregiver counted, and psychotropic medication training before she administers any such medication.`,
